WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.626
Welcome to Grade 3 English, Unit
7: Nature and the Environment.

2
00:00:04.706 --> 00:00:11.947
Unit 7 follows Amal, Nora and Teacher Yasmin from
the coast to the forest and up a mountain trail.

3
00:00:12.027 --> 00:00:18.970
Learners meet fifteen nature words, from climate
and temperature to matter, energy and planet.

4
00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:26.440
They use the present perfect to say what they have
seen, explored and visited, ask “Have you ever…?”

5
00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:32.118
questions, and build describing phrases
such as “a metal rock on the beach”.

6
00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:38.467
The unit closes with clear instructions and
a short poem about caring for our planet.

7
00:00:38.547 --> 00:00:44.743
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

8
00:00:44.823 --> 00:00:51.051
By the end of this unit, you will be able
to name and describe the beach, the coast,

9
00:00:51.131 --> 00:00:54.807
the forest and the mountain using unit vocabulary.

10
00:00:54.887 --> 00:01:02.918
You will also explain the difference between weather,
climate and temperature, and describe today's weather.

11
00:01:02.998 --> 00:01:09.978
You will also form present perfect sentences
with have or has and the correct past participle.

12
00:01:10.058 --> 00:01:12.757
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:12.837 --> 00:01:19.406
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: climate,
weather, temperature, sunshine, froze, mountain.

14
00:01:19.486 --> 00:01:24.636
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:24.716 --> 00:01:28.703
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:28.783 --> 00:01:34.165
The reading sequence includes Our Wonderful
Nature and A Poem: “Nature Is Our Home”.

17
00:01:34.245 --> 00:01:35.075
Read actively.

18
00:01:35.155 --> 00:01:39.561
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:39.641 --> 00:01:43.788
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:43.868 --> 00:01:47.599
The first language focus is The Present Perfect Tense.

21
00:01:47.679 --> 00:01:53.668
We use the present perfect for something
that happened before but still matters today.

22
00:01:53.748 --> 00:02:00.231
When you say “I have explored a forest”, you
tell people what your life has already included.

23
00:02:00.311 --> 00:02:07.923
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

24
00:02:08.003 --> 00:02:12.981
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1 — Describe a Place in Nature.

25
00:02:13.061 --> 00:02:17.754
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

26
00:02:17.834 --> 00:02:21.387
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

27
00:02:21.467 --> 00:02:25.162
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

28
00:02:25.242 --> 00:02:26.856
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:26.936 --> 00:02:34.144
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

30
00:02:34.224 --> 00:02:37.678
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

31
00:02:37.758 --> 00:02:45.850
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
